  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nRegardless of how much or any snow at all we get, the system will \nexit to our east through the day Tuesday, purging any appreciable \nmoisture while leaving us cool and dry. Hard freezes in the morning \nare looking likely mid week, so be prepared to protect any outdoor \npets and plants. Daytime temps will gradually warm through the \nThanksgiving holiday stretch, but stay near average for late \nNovember. Long range global model guidance continue to trend \npessimistically regarding any late week systems, tracking well south \nof the region on a consistent basis. Weather related impacts to \npeak holiday travel this week should be slim to none Wed through \nthe weekend, but please continue to monitor forecast updates as \nwe approach Thanksgiving. \n\nHarrel",
